{
  "name": "SYS Daily Health Check",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "cronExpression",
              "expression": "0 9 * * *"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "514793872925",
      "name": "Daily 09:00 UTC",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $env.TWENTY_BASE_URL }}/rest/automationRuns?order_by=startedAt[DescNullsLast]&limit=20",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": false
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "503252026463",
      "name": "CRM answering?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "Twenty API"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const runs = $input.first().json.data?.automationRuns || [];\n\n// 26 hours, not 24: a daily job that drifts by an hour must not raise a false\n// alarm every single morning. An alert people learn to ignore is worthless.\nconst cutoff = Date.now() - 26 * 3600_000;\nconst recent = runs.filter(r => new Date(r.startedAt).getTime() > cutoff);\n\nconst EXPECTED = ['SUB Renewal Escalation', 'OPS Scheduled Sweeps'];\nconst seen = new Set(recent.map(r => r.workflowName));\nconst missing = EXPECTED.filter(w => !seen.has(w));\nconst failed = recent.filter(r => r.status === 'FAILED');\n\nconst problems = [];\nif (missing.length) {\n  problems.push(`did not run in the last 26h: ${missing.join(', ')}`);\n}\nif (failed.length) {\n  problems.push(`${failed.length} failed run(s): ` +\n                failed.slice(0, 3).map(r => r.workflowName).join(', '));\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  healthy: problems.length === 0,\n  problems: problems.join(' | '),\n  checked: recent.length,\n}}];"
      },
      "id": "865011195768",
      "name": "Anything missing?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        560,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.healthy }}",
              "rightValue": "true",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "301401503943",
      "name": "All well?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        780,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.TWENTY_BASE_URL }}/rest/automationRuns",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": false
            }
          }
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\"workflowName\": \"SYS Daily Health Check\", \"status\": \"SUCCESS\", \"startedAt\": $execution.startedAt, \"n8nExecutionId\": $execution.id }) }}"
      },
      "id": "436664829027",
      "name": "Log run",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [
        1120,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "name": "Twenty API"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 5,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({\"channel\": \"#crm-alerts\", \"text\": `:rotating_light: *CRM automation health check failed*\n${$json.problems}\nCheck the worker first: docker compose ps worker` }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "380984391167",
      "name": "Health alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4,
      "position": [
        1120,
        490
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Ask whether yesterday actually happened\ndeploy.sh checks the worker once, on the day you deploy. Nothing\nchecks it on day forty. A dead worker means no scheduled workflow\nand no mailbox sync, and the interface stays perfectly healthy the\nwhole time \u2014 so the only way to find it is to go and look.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "648238124152",
      "name": "1. Ask whether yesterday actually happened",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        60
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Did the daily automations run?\nThree workflows are supposed to run every morning. If none of them\nleft a record in the last twenty-six hours, either the worker is\ndead, n8n's scheduler is stuck, or the CRM stopped accepting\nwrites. All three are invisible from the outside.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "490030893347",
      "name": "2. Did the daily automations run?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        540,
        80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Say something only when something is wrong\nA green tick every morning trains people to stop reading. This\nsends nothing on a good day, and names exactly what is missing on\na bad one.",
        "height": 530,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "346905413336",
      "name": "3. Say something only when something is wrong",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        120
      ]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Daily 09:00 UTC": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "CRM answering?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "CRM answering?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Anything missing?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Anything missing?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "All well?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "All well?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Log run",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "Health alert",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Health alert": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Log run",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "errorWorkflow": "SYS Error Handler"
  },
  "meta": {
    "description": "Every morning, checks that the CRM answers and that the scheduled automations actually ran yesterday. Silence is the failure mode this catches \u2014 nothing else in the stack notices absence."
  },
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "aspire"
    }
  ]
}